    "body": "<!-- pr-reviewer: c29ccd0df04bdc464cfd3af2664c093a9647fc7f -->\n**Review (M3): no blockers. This needs the maintainer, because it changes a build script** (`web/build-app-wasm.sh`; per the review-label table, a scripts change waits for the owner).\n\n**What the change does:**\n- The lock save and the `EXIT` trap move up, before the first cargo call. `cargo fetch` and the wasm-bindgen install are now covered, not only `cargo build`.\n- The trap reports a failed restore by name instead of failing silently.\n- The wasm-bindgen version is read from the saved copy (`$LOCK_KEEP`), which is correct: it comes from the tracked lock, not the rewritten one.\n- The header and the decision file both state the residual case: a SIGKILL skips the trap, and you then restore with `git checkout -- Cargo.lock`.\n\n**What I checked:**\n- `bash -n` on the new script: OK.\n- The diff touches only the script and `docs/decisions/949-wasm-script-lock.md`.\n- No product code changes.\n- The PR merges cleanly with main.\n\n**Not exercised:** a full wasm build. Note that the script does not run on stock macOS (BSD `sed -i`, and an empty array under `set -u` in bash 3.2); that is filed separately as #1315.\n",
